<title>SWITZERLAND: Swissair to adopt IAS accounts for 1996.</title>
<headline>Swissair to adopt IAS accounts for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georges Schorderet, chief financial officer for Swissair AG, said the group's accounts for the full 1996 year would be reported according to the rules set by the International Accounting Standards (IAS).</p>
<p>&quot;At the end of 1996 we will adopt IAS,&quot; Schorderet told Reuters in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>Swissair will thus report profit and losses for four divisions: Airlines, Services (which includes ground handling, technical operations, information), Cargo and Retail/Catering.</p>
<p>-- Peter Nielsen, Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
